---
// Reader: a programme owner assessing one register or connection and how to deliver it.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { describeServiceHref } from '../data/contact';
---
<Base title="Registries for digital public infrastructure | Registry Stack" description="Build reusable registry capabilities for digital public infrastructure with open-source software, documented interfaces and institutional control.">
  <SiteHeader current="dpi" />
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    <section class="hero hero-cover" aria-labelledby="dpi-title"><div class="hero-inner"><div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Digital public infrastructure</p>
      <h1 id="dpi-title">One register can support many public services.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">Connect public services to records maintained by the responsible institution. Use Registry Stack’s open-source components with your team, or work with Aubex to implement and support a service.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href={describeServiceHref('a DPI programme')} data-journey="service-inquiry">Discuss your programme</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="#shared-capabilities">See how it fits</a></div>
      <p class="hero-note">For digital-government teams, funders and implementation partners.</p>
    </div></div></section>

    <section class="section" id="shared-capabilities" aria-labelledby="reuse-title"><div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Fit with your programme</p><h2 id="reuse-title">Build a register or connect an existing source.</h2></div>
      <div class="value-grid dpi-adoption-grid">
        <article><h3>Use the records you already maintain</h3><p>Connect an existing register so authorized services can ask defined questions and receive digitally signed answers. The institution responsible for the source controls what it shares.</p><a class="inline-cta" href="/products/evidence-gateway/">Connect an existing register <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
        <article><h3>Establish a register where one is needed</h3><p>Define the records, access rules and permitted changes. Keep the current information and its history, and connect the applications that use it.</p><a class="inline-cta" href="/products/base-registry/">Manage records and history <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
      </div>
      <p class="dpi-example">For example, a health authority can maintain a facility register while a licensing service checks its recorded status. The health authority controls the information it shares; the licensing service applies its own rules. <a href="/solutions/health-and-safety/">Explore facility and oversight services</a>.</p>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section section-muted" aria-labelledby="fit-title"><div class="section-inner">
      <div class="approach-split">
        <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Implementation and support</p><h2 id="fit-title">Work with Aubex on the first service.</h2><p>We adapt and test one defined service with your team. A written pilot scope sets out the records, screens, connections, hosting and handover work, with responsibilities agreed before delivery.</p><a class="inline-cta" href="/customization/">How implementation works <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
        <div class="editorial-callout"><h3>Choose your delivery and operating team</h3><p>The core software is Apache-2.0 open source. Your institution can inspect, adapt and operate it, using its own team or another provider.</p><p>Aubex offers paid implementation and support. <a href="/pricing/">View the delivery and support options</a>.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="dpi-technical">For technical teams: <a href="https://docs.registrystack.org/start/adopt/">review the adoption paths</a>.</p>
    </div></section>

    <section class="final-cta" aria-labelledby="programme-title"><div class="section-inner"><p class="eyebrow">From programme to implementation</p><h2 id="programme-title">Discuss your first programme service.</h2><p>Tell us which records your programme needs, which services will use them and who will maintain them.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href={describeServiceHref('a DPI programme')} data-journey="service-inquiry">Discuss your programme</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/pricing/">Implementation and support</a></div></div></section>
  </main><SiteFooter />
</Base>
<style>
  .dpi-adoption-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  .dpi-example { max-width: 860px; margin: 28px 0 0; font-size: var(--type-body-sm); }
  .dpi-technical { margin: 28px 0 0; font-size: var(--type-base); }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { .dpi-adoption-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
